# Files and directories removed from the upstream expat distribution
# before it is imported into contrib/expat.  Derived from FreeBSD's
# contrib/expat/FREEBSD-Xlist.
#
# Entries are spelled out rather than globbed.  The glob patterns this
# list used to carry were unsafe or dead:
#
#   *.pc.in     matched expat.pc.in, which we ship -- applying the list
#               literally deleted a file that belongs in the tree
#   *.cmake     matches lib/libexpat.def.cmake, which we keep, whenever
#   *config.h   this list is fed to a matcher that descends into
#               subdirectories (tar -X, find); likewise lib/winconfig.h
#   *.MPW *.def *.dsp *.dsw *.vcxproj* Configure* CMake* amiga bcb5 vms
#   expat.sln doc/valid-xhtml10.png
#               matched nothing as of 2.8.3; upstream dropped them long
#               ago
#
# Deliberately kept despite looking like candidates: expat.pc.in,
# expat_config.h.in, lib/libexpat.def.cmake and lib/winconfig.h.
#
# This list is a description of the trim, not the authority on it.
# Verify an import by diffing the trimmed file set against the previous
# vendor tag and requiring them to be identical apart from genuinely new
# upstream files.
